/.devbox/
/.direnv/
/.idea/
/.task/
/coverage.out
# A Go workspace is for editing this module and minecraft-protocol together. It
# never belongs in a commit: CI resolves what go.mod pins, and a workspace that
# reached the runner would build a neighbouring working tree instead of the
# released version, so a stale pin would pass here and ship.
/go.work
/go.work.sum
/reference/work/
*.jar
*.class
*.java
# The oracle harnesses are ours: they supply a block lookup, a minimal entity,
# and a text protocol, and they reimplement no game logic. They are committed so
# that anyone with a prepared workspace can re-run the differential gates, which
# is what makes those gates a check rather than a claim. Decompiled sources and
# jars stay ignored above and below.
!internal/oracle/java/*.java
*.tiny
*.tsrg
*.srg
*.csrg
